## test the driver using cat and echo

1) first insert the driver and check your sysfs file /sys/kernel/etx_sysfs/etx_value

2) read using cat
$ sudo cat /sys/kernel/etx_sysfs/etx_value

3) write using echo 
$ sudo echo 123 > /sys/kernel/etx_sysfs/etx_value


## if you get any error like below 
$ sudo echo 123 > /sys/kernel/etx_sysfs/etx_value 
bash: /sys/kernel/etx_sysfs/etx_value: Permission denied

solution: change the sysfs file permission
$ sudo chmod -R 666 /sys/kernel/etx_sysfs/etx_value

## after use remove the driver 
